# weather prediction system estimates the probabilities of three possible conditions as 
sunny, rainy, and cloudy: P=[0.6, 0.3, 0.1]. The system needs to measure the uncertainty in its 
predictions. 
Write a Python program to calculate the entropy of the probability distribution and to display 
the probabilities of the three weather conditions in a bar chart.



import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

P = np.array([0.6,0.3,0.1])
H = -np.sum(P*np.log2(P))
print("Entropy:", H)
plt.bar(["Sunny","Rainy","Cloudy"],P)
plt.show()
